31x + 28y &= -32 \\
y &= \frac{-32 - 31x}{28}
\end{align*}

Now we have expressions for both $y$ and $z$ in terms of $x$. Substitute these expressions into the first equation to solve for $x$:
\begin{align*}
x - 9\left(\frac{-32 - 31x}{28}\right) + 7\left(\frac{9 + 4y}{31}\right) &= 1 \\
x + \frac{288 + 279x}{28} + \frac{63 + 28y}{31} &= 1 \\
