    if command[0] == "CREATE":
        title = command[1]
        content = command[2]
        author = command[3]
        post = create_post(title, content, author)
        print(json.dumps(post))
    elif command[0] == "READALL":
        print(json.dumps(read_all_posts()))
    elif command[0] == "READ":
        id = int(command[1])
        post = read_post(id)
        print(json.dumps(post))
    elif command[0] == "UPDATE":
        id = int(command[1])
        title = command[2]
        content = command[3]
        author = command[4]
        post = update_post(id, title, content, author)
        print(json.dumps(post))
    elif command[0] == "DELETE":
        id = int(command[1])
        print(json.dumps(delete_post(id)))
```

The Python program simulates a blog post management system. It uses a list `posts` to store blog posts as dictionaries. Functions are defined for each CRUD operation. `CREATE` adds a new post, `READ` retrieves a post by ID, `READALL` retrieves all posts, `UPDATE` modifies a post, and `DELETE` removes a post. The program takes commands from standard input and outputs JSON responses using the `json` module.
